// Where the candidate's latency actually comes from, per version.
//
// ADVISORY ONLY. These are server-side OpenTelemetry spans emitted by the
// checkout service itself. They are NOT the contract evidence: the verifier
// scores client-observed results from sloproof-requests, and its scoped
// credential is refused (HTTP 403) on this data stream by design.
//
// The service emits two spans per request: "POST /checkout" (the request) and
// "checkout -> quote" (the simulated in-process dependency). Comparing them
// shows how much of the request is spent in the dependency -- the "why" behind
// a p95 that the contract can only report as a number.
//
// The dependency span is matched by the frozen window plus its own label rather
// than by run_id, because images built before the run labels were added to the
// child span carry only sloproof.simulated_dependency. One trial runs at a
// time, so the frozen window is an adequate advisory scope; it is not a
// cohort-exact filter and no verdict depends on it.
//
// duration is nanoseconds; divide to milliseconds.
//
// Params: ?run_id, ?window_start, ?window_end
FROM traces-generic.otel-default
| WHERE @timestamp >= ?window_start AND @timestamp < ?window_end
    AND (attributes.sloproof.run_id == ?run_id
         OR attributes.sloproof.simulated_dependency == true)
| EVAL ms = duration / 1000000.0
| STATS spans  = COUNT(*),
        errors = SUM(CASE(status.code == "Error", 1, 0)),
        p50_ms = PERCENTILE(ms, 50),
        p95_ms = PERCENTILE(ms, 95)
      BY name, resource.attributes.service.version
| SORT `resource.attributes.service.version`, name
